From d7995db4ce867716e82787b8eb99d125842892e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "A.R." <boldaxolotl@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Add a default arm to the AXI DMA read-request count case

The rd_req_count_for_payload_next case already lists all eight selector
values, so the default arm is unreachable for 2-state inputs and behavior
is unchanged. Without it, the slang-based Yosys frontend does not detect
the case as full and infers a hold-value combinational loop
(https://github.com/povik/sv-elab/issues/387). Needed only for ASIC
synthesis; simulation and lint pass without it.
---
 src/axi/rtl/axi_dma_ctrl.sv | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/axi/rtl/axi_dma_ctrl.sv b/src/axi/rtl/axi_dma_ctrl.sv
index 80d4ef38..ff3e583b 100644
--- a/src/axi/rtl/axi_dma_ctrl.sv
+++ b/src/axi/rtl/axi_dma_ctrl.sv
@@ -651,6 +651,10 @@ import kv_defines_pkg::*;
             3'b101: rd_req_count_for_payload_next = rd_req_count_for_payload - 1;
             3'b110: rd_req_count_for_payload_next = rd_req_count_for_payload; // Don't queue new requests when current requests are pending
             3'b111: rd_req_count_for_payload_next = rd_req_count_for_payload - 1; // Don't queue new requests when current requests are pending
+            // Unreachable for 2-state selectors (all 8 values are listed above). Without it the
+            // yosys-slang frontend does not detect the case as full and emits a hold-value
+            // combinational loop (povik/sv-elab#387).
+            default: rd_req_count_for_payload_next = rd_req_count_for_payload;
         endcase
     end
 
